        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.101,
            0.486,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.154,
            0.744,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Handpicking is used for separating solid materials on the basis of differences in size, colour and shape from a mixture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.203,
            0.743,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The process in which the stalks are beaten to separate grains from them is called threshing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.25,
            0.743,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The method of separating lighter husk from heavier grains by wind or blowing air is called winnowing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.299,
            0.743,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The process of separating solids from a mixture based on variations in particle size using a sieve is called sieving."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.347,
            0.743,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Evaporation is the process in which a liquid gets converted into its vapour. It can be used to separate a solid dissolved in a liquid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.414,
            0.744,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The process of settling down of heavier insoluble component at the bottom of a liquid is called sedimentation. When the liquid is removed by tilting the vessel, the process is called decantation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.499,
            0.743,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Filtration can be used to separate insoluble solid components from a liquid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.547,
            0.604,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Churning is used to extract butter from curd."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.576,
            0.743,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Separation of magnetic and non-magnetic substances by using a magnet is called magnetic separation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.625,
            0.376,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Play a Game—WISE FISH"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.655,
            0.744,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Prepare your own fishing rod with locally available eco-friendly materials. Tie a thread to one end of the rod and a magnet to the free end of the thread. The Tank 1 has red cardboard fish and Tank 2 has blue cardboard slips attached to iron clips. Fish out a red fish representing the method of separation first and then fish out one blue slip related to the red one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.776,
            0.689,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Watch out for your friends. Are they fishing out correctly?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.874,
            0.755,
            0.914,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in Everyday Life Methods of Separation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
